course: dictionary
lesson: 8333
title: Roman with a capital R
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change meaning with a capital letter. «Paul wrote letters to churches, such as Romans and Corinthians.» Here Romans with a capital R is a name, so it is about people or writings from ancient Rome. Look at the capital letter and the words near it.
explain: Roman can also describe things. «Roman roads» and «Roman numerals» are roads and numbers that belong to the Romans long ago. When Roman is a describing word, it tells you where something comes from. Ask yourself: is this thing connected with ancient Rome?
explain: Roman with a small r means something different. It is the name for ordinary upright print, the normal letters you are reading now, not italic slanted print. A small r tells you the word is about printing, not about people. Always check the letter before you choose a meaning.
fact: A capital R in Roman usually means connected with ancient Rome, or a person from there.
fact: «Romans» with a capital R means people from ancient Rome or the city of Rome today.
fact: «Roman numerals» use the letters I, V, X, L, C, D and M.
fact: «Roman» with a small r means ordinary upright print, not italic.
fact: «Writing came to Britain with the Romans about 2,000 years ago.»
exercise: In «the Roman Empire», what does Roman mean? | A kind of coin you can spend today | *Connected with ancient Rome | Ordinary upright print | A small type of biscuit
exercise: Which letters are used in Roman numerals? | *I, V, X, L, C, D and M | A, B, C and D | 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5
exercise: «Writing came to Britain with the Romans about 2,000 years ago.» Who are the Romans here? | *People from ancient Rome | Shopkeepers in Rome today | Stone Age people
test: What does a Roman mean in «a Roman soldier»? | A small type of print | Something made of wood | A kind of Roman numeral | *Connected with ancient Rome
test: What kind of print is roman with a small r? | Handwriting | Italic | *Ordinary upright print | Bold
exam: Which Roman numeral means 5? | I | X | M | *V
